.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt VFS_MKDIR 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_mkdir
.Nd create a directory in the virtual file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vfs/vfs.h
.Ft int
.Fn vfs_mkdir "const char *path" "uint16_t permission"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_mkdir
function attempts to create a new directory at the location specified by
.Fa path .
.Pp
If
.Fa path
is an absolute path (starts with '/'), the lookup and creation occur relative to the filesystem root node
.Pq Va fs_root .
.Pp
If
.Fa path
is a relative path, the lookup and creation occur relative to the current process's working directory
.Pq Va current_process->cwd_node .
If the current process or its CWD is not set (e.g., during early boot), it falls back to the filesystem root.
.Pp
The
.Fa permission
argument specifies the permission bits (mode) for the new directory.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn vfs_mkdir
function returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure (e.g., if the parent directory is not found, or the underlying filesystem does not support directory creation).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs 9 ,
.Xr vfs_lookup 9 ,
.Xr vfs_mount 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn vfs_mkdir
function appeared in Substrate.
